{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487579631,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMDg4MTM2NTA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1314","origin":"github"},"title":"git-annex-status to ignore submodules","message":"A call to either `git status` or `git annex status` can be very expensive in large submodule hierarchies. For `git status` there's `--ignore-submodules`, which can be used to examine just the repository we are in without inspecting its submodules. Since this is way faster while it often provides all we actually need, I'd love to see that option for `git annex status`, too.\nAny chance to get this, @joeyh ?\n\nIn a way, this might be related to how to fix http://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/git_annex_status_fails_with_submodule_in_direct_mode/","files":null}]}